 {:seon.task/name "a-flush-costs-the-children-that-changed"
  :seon.task/plan "From the managing session's audit (2026-11-10, per-turn costs): a flush of a list component walks every child it holds, cache hits included, so one changed child costs the list O(children): measured 27k ticks at 10 children, 326k at 100 (seon.render/flush! and seon.render/emit's cache-hit path, a lookup a member). It should cost the children that changed plus O(1) for the list. Learn first: what jolt/incr (retired) measured and its delta-interface notes, and seon.render/render!'s hit path. Proof, red first: a cost proof that grows the unchanged children (10, 40, 160) with one child changed, ticks flat within its bound. Not before stage 2a lands (docs/users.md#the-stages-agreed-2026-11-09)."
